VALIDATION ONLY: the RAM half of translate_icache_sync publishes nothing
(new RAM-cache code is never written back or invalidated).  The checker must
flag it; restoring the sync must silence it.
Since code-health A-6 (JIT_CODE_DISCIPLINE built in) the legacy sync exists
only as JIT_CODE_AB's verbatim copy, jit_legacy_icache_sync, so this patches
that copy and bites only in a JIT_CODE_AB build running a legacy jit_code_mode.
The results in docs/JIT-COHERENCY.md were taken on the non-discipline twin.
--- a/cpu_threaded.c
+++ b/cpu_threaded.c
@@ -549,9 +549,9 @@
         platform_cache_sync(last_rom_translation_ptr, rom_translation_ptr);
         last_rom_translation_ptr = rom_translation_ptr;
     }
     if (last_ram_translation_ptr < ram_translation_ptr) {
         jit_code_stats.publishes++;
-        platform_cache_sync(last_ram_translation_ptr, ram_translation_ptr);
+        /* JITCOH VALIDATION: sync removed */
         last_ram_translation_ptr = ram_translation_ptr;
     }
 }
